---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
import TeamBuilder from '../../components/TeamBuilder';
import { defaultFormat } from '../../data/formats';
---
<BaseLayout title="Gen 9 National Dex Casual Team Builder | Super Pokémon Team Builder" description="Plan a casual Pokémon team from 1,025 base species with Generation 9 typing, transparent scores and computed teammate recommendations."><SiteHeader/><main id="main"><p class="eyebrow">ONE CLEAR STARTING FORMAT</p><h1>Gen 9 National Dex Casual Team Builder</h1><p class="intro">Use Generation 9 data to plan a casual team across the first nine generations.</p><TeamBuilder client:load/><section class="seo-content"><h2>What is in this pool?</h2><p>{defaultFormat.description}</p><p>Earlier species are retained even if they are not available in Scarlet or Violet. The tool does not apply tier bans, restricted-species limits or official event regulations. Its role is to help compare team typing and base stats.</p><h3>Generation 9 assumptions</h3><p>The 18 standard attacking types use the Generation 9 type chart. The type matrix assumes no abilities, moves, items or battle transformations. Stellar and Terastallization are not modeled.</p><h3>Build and compare</h3><p>Search by English name or Pokédex number, filter by type and generation, and choose a replacement slot to compare candidate scores.</p></section></main><SiteFooter/></BaseLayout>
